---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
import HowEngageEngineWorks from '../components/HowEngageEngineWorks.astro'
// Rebuilt 2026-10-30 (Robbie): holds the depth cut from the homepage trim. Copy moved verbatim
// from index.astro. The Oct-1 five-layer version is in git history.
---
<Base
  title="How It Works | Marketing Performance Group"
  description="How the Demand Collapse Diagnostic™ and EngageEngine™ find where home-service demand is lost, and recover it."
>
  <nav class="mp-nav">
    <div class="mp-nav-inner">
      <a href="/" class="mp-logo">
        <img src="/mp-logo-v3.png" alt="Marketing Performance, Powered by EngageEngine™" width="217" height="44" />
      </a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <main class="mp">

    <!-- ═══ 2. PROBLEM (Hormozi §2): symptoms, failed attempts, the real enemy ═══ -->
    <section class="mp-problem">
      <div class="mp-problem-inner">
        <p class="mp-eye">The Problem</p>
        <h2 class="mp-h2">Most businesses don't lose work because people aren't interested.</h2>
        <div class="mp-problem-prose">
          <p>They lose it when confidence collapses <em>after</em> interest, under decision pressure. It usually looks like plenty of activity with no predictable outcome, results that swing month to month with nobody able to explain why, and advice to add more: more ads, more posts, more spend. Nobody tells you what's actually broken.</p>
          <p>That isn't a tactics problem. It's a confidence problem. And it happens in a small number of specific places, which is the useful part: if there are only a few places it can break, you can go find out which one it is instead of guessing.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="mp-problem-punch">That's the first thing I do. Not execution. Not a campaign. Identifying where confidence is collapsing between interest and decision. Once that's clear the correction is usually straightforward. Until it's clear, everything else is guessing.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 2b. The four places demand disappears -->
    <section class="mp-breaks">
      <div class="mp-breaks-inner">
        <p class="mp-eye" data-animate>The Four Moments</p>
        <h2 class="mp-h2" data-animate data-delay="0.05">There are only a few places a sale can break.</h2>
        <p class="mp-breaks-lede" data-animate data-delay="0.1">Nearly every revenue problem I see comes down to one of four moments.</p>
        <div class="mp-breaks-list" data-animate data-delay="0.15">
          <div class="mp-break"><p class="mp-break-fm">Not Seen When the Decision Is Made</p><h3>You weren't there when they decided.</h3><p>People were looking for what you do. You just weren't in front of them at the moment they picked somebody.</p></div>
          <div class="mp-break"><p class="mp-break-fm">Seen But Not Trusted</p><h3>They found you and didn't trust you yet.</h3><p>They looked, and they left. The interest was real. The confidence wasn't.</p></div>
          <div class="mp-break"><p class="mp-break-fm">Trusted But Still Compared</p><h3>They trusted you and shopped you anyway.</h3><p>You gave the estimate, they compared, and you lost some you should have won, usually on price, because the difference between you and the other fellow never got made clear.</p></div>
          <div class="mp-break"><p class="mp-break-fm">Selected But No Action</p><h3>They meant to hire you and never got to it.</h3><p>They said they'd call back, and they meant it. Most of those jobs aren't lost. They're stuck.</p></div>
        </div>
        <p class="mp-breaks-foot" data-animate data-delay="0.2">Different problems, different fixes, and the fix for one does nothing for the other three.</p>
        <div class="mp-breaks-turn" data-animate data-delay="0.25">
          <p><strong>Here's the trouble.</strong> From where you sit, you can only see one of the four. You know about the estimates you lost. You don't know about the people who never came back, never called, or never found you at all.</p>
          <p class="mp-couplet">More advertising doesn't fix lost demand.<br />Finding the failure point does.</p>
          <p>The Demand Collapse Diagnostic&trade; looks at all four, not by asking you to guess, but by reading what your own numbers already say: where you land when somebody nearby is choosing, what people do on your site before they leave, what they type before they hire, and who came looking and never called.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══ 3. SOLUTION (Hormozi §3): the named mechanism ═══ -->
    <section class="mp-mech">
      <div class="mp-mech-inner">
        <p class="mp-eye" data-animate>The Solution</p>
        <h2 class="mp-h2" data-animate data-delay="0.05">Diagnose first. Then deploy.</h2>
        <div class="mp-mech-grid" data-animate data-delay="0.1">
          <div class="mp-mech-step"><span class="mp-mech-n">01</span><h3>Diagnose</h3><p>Find where demand is disappearing across the four failure modes.</p></div>
          <div class="mp-mech-step"><span class="mp-mech-n">02</span><h3>Detect</h3><p>Use buyer-signal intelligence to understand where demand is forming and where buyers are moving toward a decision.</p></div>
          <div class="mp-mech-step"><span class="mp-mech-n">03</span><h3>Recover</h3><p>Use EngageEngine&trade; to coordinate advertising, follow-up, visibility and conversion around the confirmed failure point.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="mp-mech-note" data-animate data-delay="0.15">
          <p><strong>EngageEngine&trade;</strong> applies enterprise-grade buyer-signal intelligence to a single local market, helping us recognize when demand is forming, where buyers are in the decision process and what should happen next.</p>
          <p class="mp-mech-punch">See demand forming earlier. Reach buyers sooner. Lose fewer jobs between interest and action.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 3b. How EngageEngine works (the journey graphic) -->
    <HowEngageEngineWorks />

    <!-- 4c. Recent catches -->
    <section class="mp-catch">
      <div class="mp-catch-inner">
        <p class="mp-eye" data-animate>After the Launch</p>
        <h2 class="mp-h2" data-animate data-delay="0.05">We catch it before it costs you.</h2>
        <p class="mp-catch-lede" data-animate data-delay="0.1">Campaigns don't fail loudly. They fail quietly, in ways you'd never see on an invoice. Every account gets watched every week. Recent catches:</p>
        <ul class="mp-catch-list" data-animate data-delay="0.15">
          <li>A plumbing client's campaign delivery collapsed 90% overnight. Caught the same day, diagnosed as a campaign issue, not a market issue, and restored. Conversions never dipped.</li>
          <li>An email campaign started silently dropping one in four sends. Caught before the next send went out, fixed before the client ever saw it.</li>
          <li>Visitors on three client sites were clicking buttons that didn't respond, at the exact moment they were trying to act. Found it in the behavior recordings. Fixed it.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mp-catch-foot" data-animate data-delay="0.2">The launch is the easy part. The watching is what you're paying for.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ: objections handled right before the final ask -->
    <section class="mp-faq">
      <div class="mp-faq-inner">
        <h2 class="mp-h2">Questions</h2>
        <details class="mp-faq-item"><summary>Is the plan really free?</summary><p>Yes. Qualified companies in available territories receive the plan without paying for it. You keep the plan whether you implement it yourself or ask Marketing Performance Group to help.</p></details>
        <details class="mp-faq-item"><summary>Why do I have to qualify?</summary><p>Every plan is researched and prepared for a specific company and market. The review is designed for established home-service companies where the findings can support a meaningful recovery plan.</p></details>
        <details class="mp-faq-item"><summary>Is the scorecard the complete diagnosis?</summary><p>No. The twelve questions identify the first failure point to investigate. The personalized review examines the company, market, competitive position and available evidence before the plan is prepared.</p></details>
        <details class="mp-faq-item"><summary>Do I have to hire Marketing Performance Group afterward?</summary><p>No. The plan is yours. You may implement it yourself. If you want Marketing Performance Group to implement it through EngageEngine&trade;, that conversation happens only after you have seen the plan.</p></details>
        <details class="mp-faq-item"><summary>What information do you need?</summary><p>The application asks for basic company information, your website, trade, service area and current challenge. Robbie begins with publicly available information and the answers you provide. Any request for additional access should be explained and approved separately.</p></details>
        <details class="mp-faq-item"><summary>What if my territory is already claimed?</summary><p>Marketing Performance Group works with one company per trade, per market. If a direct competitor has already claimed the territory, Robbie will tell you before preparing the full plan.</p></details>
        <details class="mp-faq-item"><summary>How is EngageEngine&trade; different from ordinary advertising?</summary><p>Ordinary advertising usually starts with channels and budgets. EngageEngine&trade; starts with the confirmed failure point, applies buyer-signal intelligence to the local market and coordinates the work around where demand is actually being lost.</p></details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mp-close">
      <h2 class="mp-close-h1" data-animate>Is your territory still open?</h2>
      <p class="mp-close-h2" data-animate data-delay="0.05">Find out in twelve questions.</p>
      <div class="mp-close-cta" data-animate data-delay="0.2">
        <a href="/diagnostic/" class="mp-btn-primary" data-plan-cta="how-it-works">Get Your Five-Part Demand Recovery Plan</a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
  <Footer ctaHref="/diagnostic/" />
</Base>

<style>
  /* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     APPLE-FIDELITY HOMEPAGE. Hormozi rewrite v2.
     Tokens: Canvas White #f5f5f7 / Pure White #ffffff /
     Midnight Graphite #1d1d1f / Mid Gray #707070 /
     Interactive Blue #0071e3 / Border Silver #d6d6d6.
     Cards 0px radius. Images 8px. Buttons 980px pill.
     Shadow XL: rgba(0,0,0,0.22) 3px 5px 30px 0px.
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

  /* ─── Top nav (logo only) ─── */
  .mp-nav {
    position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 100;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.72);
    backdrop-filter: saturate(180%) blur(20px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: saturate(180%) blur(20px);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .mp-nav-inner {
    max-width: 1280px; margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 32px; height: 56px;
    display: flex; align-items: center;
  }
  .mp-logo {
    display: flex; align-items: center;
    min-height: 44px; text-decoration: none;
  }
  .mp-logo img { height: 44px; width: auto; display: block; }
  .mp-logo:hover { text-decoration: none; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .mp-logo img { height: 34px; }
  }

  /* ─── Page base ─── */
  .mp { background: var(--canvas); color: var(--graphite); }
  .mp h1, .mp h2 { font-family: var(--font-d); color: var(--graphite); }
  .mp p { color: var(--graphite); }
  .mp em { font-style: italic; }

  /* ─── Primary button (Apple Interactive Blue pill) ─── */
  .mp-btn-primary {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;
    background: var(--blue); color: #fff;
    font-family: var(--font-t); font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -0.022em;
    padding: 12px 24px; border-radius: 980px;
    text-decoration: none; transition: background 0.2s;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .mp-btn-primary:hover { background: var(--blue-link); text-decoration: none; color: #fff; }
  .mp-btn-primary::after {
    content: "→"; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1;
    transition: transform 0.2s;
  }
  .mp-btn-primary:hover::after { transform: translateX(3px); }

  /* ─── Eyebrows + headings ─── */
  .mp-eye {
    font-family: var(--font-t);
    font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--blue); margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .mp-h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-d);
    font-size: clamp(36px, 4.4vw, 56px);
    font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.022em; color: var(--graphite);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .mp-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-d);
    font-size: clamp(30px, 3.8vw, 44px);
    font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.018em; color: var(--graphite);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    max-width: 780px;
  }
  .mp-lede {
    font-family: var(--font-t);
    font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: -0.022em; color: var(--mid-gray);
    max-width: 680px;
  }
  .mp-micro {
    font-family: var(--font-t);
    font-size: 13px; color: var(--light-gray);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }
  .mp-micro strong { color: var(--graphite); font-weight: 600; }
  .mp-section-head { margin-bottom: 48px; }
  .mp-section-head.mp-center,
  .mp-h2.mp-center,
  .mp-eye.mp-center { text-align: center; }
  .mp-section-head.mp-center .mp-h2,
  .mp-section-head.mp-center .mp-lede { margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
  .mp-h2.mp-center { margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }

  /* ─── 1. HERO ─── */
  .mp-hero {
    padding: 80px 32px 100px;
    background: var(--canvas);
  }
  .mp-hero-grid {
    max-width: 1320px; margin: 0 auto;
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 56px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .mp-hero-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(360px, 520px) minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 64px;
    }
  }
  .mp-hero-copy { max-width: 540px; }
  .mp-hero-prose {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
    max-width: 540px;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  .mp-hero-prose p {
    font-family: var(--font-t);
    font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.55;
    letter-spacing: -0.022em;
    color: var(--mid-gray);
  }
  .mp-hero-cta-block {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start;
  }

  /* Snapshot artifact. Actual product screenshot, framed Apple-style. */
  .mp-artifact {
    margin: 0;
    justify-self: stretch; width: 100%;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px;
  }
  .mp-artifact-img {
    width: 100%; height: auto; display: block;
    border-radius: 8px;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-xl, rgba(0,0,0,0.22) 3px 5px 30px 0px);
    background: var(--white);
  }
  .mp-artifact-cap {
    font-family: var(--font-t);
    font-size: 12px; font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--light-gray);
    text-align: center;
  }
  @media (max-width: 1023px) {
    .mp-artifact { max-width: 100%; }
  }

  /* Hero VSL — vertical 9:16 (2026-10-01), capped so it never towers over the hero copy */
  .mp-hero-video {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 280px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    background: #1d1d1f;
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
    aspect-ratio: 9 / 16;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-xl, rgba(0,0,0,0.22) 3px 5px 30px 0px);
  }
  .mp-hero-video video { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; object-fit: cover; }
  .mp-hero-video--wide { max-width: 640px; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; }
  .mp-hero-video--slot {
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; text-align: center;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, #f5f5f7 0 12px, #e8e8ed 12px 24px);
    border: 2px dashed #b0b0b5; box-shadow: none;
    font-family: var(--font-t); font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--mid-gray);
  }
  @media (max-width: 768px) { .mp-hero-video { max-width: 280px; } }

  /* Proof-card styles now live in ProofCards.astro (shared by / and /snapshot). */
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    /* The video stays on mobile, capped at 280px wide so it does not bury the case studies. */
    .mp-hero { padding-bottom: 8px; }
  }

  /* ─── 4b. CATCH ─── */
  .mp-catch { padding: 110px 32px; background: var(--white); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .mp-catch-inner { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .mp-catch-lede {
    font-family: var(--font-t); font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.5;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--mid-gray); margin-bottom: 34px;
  }
  .mp-catch-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 34px; }
  .mp-catch-list li {
    font-family: var(--font-t); font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em; color: var(--graphite);
    padding: 20px 0 20px 34px; position: relative;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .mp-catch-list li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .mp-catch-list li::before {
    content: ''; position: absolute; left: 4px; top: 29px;
    width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--blue, #0071e3);
  }
  .mp-catch-foot {
    font-family: var(--font-t); font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em; color: var(--graphite);
  }

  /* ─── 2. PROBLEM ─── */
  .mp-problem {
    padding: 112px 32px;
    background: var(--white);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .mp-problem-inner {
    max-width: 780px; margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .mp-problem-prose {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px;
    margin: 28px 0 36px;
  }
  .mp-problem-prose p {
    font-family: var(--font-t);
    font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: -0.018em;
    color: var(--mid-gray);
  }
  .mp-problem-prose p strong {
    color: var(--graphite); font-weight: 600;
  }
  .mp-problem-punch {
    font-family: var(--font-d);
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2.4vw, 26px);
    font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--graphite);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--blue);
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }

  /* ─── 3. SOLUTION ─── */
  .mp-solution {
    padding: 112px 32px;
    background: var(--canvas);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .mp-solution-inner {
    max-width: 780px; margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .mp-solution-prose {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px;
    margin-top: 28px;
  }
  .mp-solution-prose p {
    font-family: var(--font-t);
    font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: -0.018em;
    color: var(--graphite);
  }
  .mp-solution-prose p strong {
    color: var(--blue); font-weight: 600;
  }
  .mp-solution-more {
    margin-top: 32px;
    font-family: var(--font-t);
    font-size: 15px;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }
  .mp-text-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: baseline; gap: 6px;
    color: var(--blue-link);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }
  .mp-text-link:hover { color: var(--blue); }
  .mp-text-link-arrow {
    display: inline-block;
    transition: transform 0.2s;
  }
  .mp-text-link:hover .mp-text-link-arrow {
    transform: translateX(3px);
  }

  /* ─── 4. PROOF ─── */
  .mp-proof-section {
    padding: 112px 32px;
    background: var(--white);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .mp-proof-block {
    max-width: 780px; margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .mp-proof-feature {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 24px;
    padding: 28px 32px;
    background: var(--canvas);
    margin: 32px 0 40px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--blue);
  }
  .mp-anchor-photo {
    width: 80px; height: 80px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--canvas);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    font-family: var(--font-d);
    font-size: 22px; font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--mid-gray);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .mp-anchor-photo img {
    width: 100%; height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }
  .mp-anchor-attr {
    font-family: var(--font-t);
    font-size: 14px; color: var(--mid-gray);
    margin-bottom: 8px; letter-spacing: -0.018em;
  }
  .mp-anchor-attr strong { color: var(--graphite); font-weight: 600; }
  .mp-anchor-stats {
    font-family: var(--font-t);
    font-size: 13px; color: var(--blue-link);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px;
  }
  .mp-anchor-stats strong { font-weight: 600; }
  .mp-dot { color: var(--light-gray); }
  .mp-proof-stack {
    list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 22px;
  }
  .mp-proof-stack > li {
    font-family: var(--font-t);
    font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55;
    letter-spacing: -0.018em;
    color: var(--graphite);
    padding-left: 24px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .mp-proof-stack > li::before {
    content: "→";
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0;
    color: var(--blue); font-weight: 700;
  }
  .mp-proof-stack > li strong { font-weight: 600; }
  .mp-proof-founder {
    display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 18px;
    padding: 22px 24px;
    background: var(--canvas);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--blue);
  }
  .mp-proof-founder::before { display: none; }
  .mp-proof-founder-photo {
    width: 72px; height: 72px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    object-fit: cover; object-position: top;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    box-shadow: rgba(0,0,0,0.12) 2px 3px 14px 0px;
  }
  .mp-proof-founder-quote {
    font-family: var(--font-d);
    font-size: 17px; font-style: italic; line-height: 1.45;
    letter-spacing: -0.018em;
    color: var(--graphite);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .mp-proof-founder-attr {
    font-family: var(--font-t);
    font-size: 13px; color: var(--mid-gray);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }
  .mp-proof-founder-attr strong { color: var(--graphite); font-weight: 600; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .mp-proof-feature { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }
    .mp-proof-founder { flex-direction: column; }
  }

  /* ─── 5. VALUE STACK ─── */
  .mp-offer {
    padding: 112px 32px;
    background: var(--canvas);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .mp-offer-inner {
    max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .mp-stack {
    list-style: none; padding: 0;
    margin: 40px 0 32px;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1px;
    background: var(--border);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .mp-stack-item {
    background: var(--white);
    padding: 32px 36px;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px;
  }
  .mp-stack-head {
    font-family: var(--font-d);
    font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.018em; line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--graphite);
  }
  .mp-stack-body {
